# Implementation Plan - Teacher Module: Create Assessment Questions

This plan outlines the design and implementation of assessment question creation, editing, and image upload functionality for the teacher's dashboard.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Database Schema Update**: We will add a nullable `image_url` column to the `questions` table. If the environment restricts database migration commands from the agent shell, we will execute a raw SQL query `ALTER TABLE questions ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS image_url TEXT;` through a temporary Next.js server runner to apply it successfully.

> [!NOTE]
> **Storage for Uploads**: Question images will be uploaded and stored locally in the `public/uploads/` directory of the application server. This is self-contained and avoids external cloud storage dependencies.

## Proposed Changes

We will group the changes into: schema modification, server actions, api routes, and UI page additions.

---

### Database Skema

#### [MODIFY] [schema.ts](file:///c:/Semester/version%20Skripsi/v1/src/db/schema.ts)
- Add `imageUrl: text('image_url')` to the `questions` table definition:
```typescript
export const questions = pgTable('questions', {
  id: uuid('id').defaultRandom().primaryKey(),
  assessmentId: uuid('assessment_id').notNull().references(() => assessments.id),
  questionText: text('question_text').notNull(),
  questionType: varchar('question_type', { length: 30 }).notNull(), // 'multiple_choice' | 'true_false' | 'essay'
  options: jsonb('options'),
  correctAnswer: varchar('correct_answer', { length: 255 }).notNull(),
  imageUrl: text('image_url'),
});
```

